
<section class="phase-page">

    <h1>Test Analysis</h1>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
            During the Test Analysis phase, I analyzed selected
            functionalities of the Automation Exercise website
            to identify testable conditions, expected behaviors,
            and potential risks before designing test cases.
        </p>
        <p>
            Test conditions were identified based on the
            application's visible features and expected
            user interactions.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Functional Analysis</h2>
        <p>
            Four main functional areas were selected for testing.
        </p>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>User Registration</h3>
                <p>
                    Analyze account creation, required fields,
                    existing email handling, and input validation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>User Login</h3>
                <p>
                    Analyze authentication behavior using
                    valid and invalid login credentials.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Product Search</h3>
                <p>
                    Analyze how the website responds to
                    exact, partial, and unmatched search terms.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Shopping Cart</h3>
                <p>
                    Analyze adding products, quantities,
                    calculated totals, and empty cart behavior.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Identified Test Conditions</h2>

        <ul class="goals-list">
            <li>Registration with new account information.</li>
            <li>Registration using an existing email address.</li>
            <li>Validation of registration field inputs.</li>
            <li>Login with valid and invalid credentials.</li>
            <li>Search using exact and partial product names.</li>
            <li>Search using a term with no matching products.</li>
            <li>Add products to the shopping cart.</li>
            <li>Verify product quantities and displayed totals.</li>
            <li>Verify cart behavior after removing products.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Data Analysis</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Valid Data</h3>
                <p>
                    Correct account information, valid login
                    credentials, existing product names,
                    and supported product quantities.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Invalid Data</h3>
                <p>
                    Incorrect login credentials, duplicate
                    email addresses, and invalid registration
                    field values.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Special Conditions</h3>
                <p>
                    Partial search terms, searches without
                    matching results, and an empty shopping cart.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Risk Analysis</h2>

        <p>
            The following potential risks were considered
            when selecting and prioritizing test conditions:
        </p>

        <ul class="goals-list">
            <li>Invalid user information may be accepted.</li>
            <li>Authentication errors may affect account access.</li>
            <li>Search results may not match user expectations.</li>
            <li>Cart quantities or displayed totals may be incorrect.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            These represent potential risks to investigate,
            not confirmed defects.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Analysis Output</h2>

        <p>
            The identified test conditions provided the
            foundation for the next phase, Test Design,
            where detailed test cases, test steps,
            expected results, and priorities were defined.
        </p>
    </section>

</section>
